{"h":3390,"lines":[{"x":0.092019397332742697,"t":"Test 3","y":0.044306904107856648,"h":0.018944331256337654,"c":1,"w":0.066474552154541011},{"t":"READING","w":0.13373582204182949,"h":0.019859010139397837,"c":1,"y":0.091087936598409192,"x":0.44339902896130162},{"x":0.092402467477720809,"y":0.15250737501648404,"w":0.31006159464518229,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","c":1,"h":0.01900425238595238},{"h":0.021802324953332453,"x":0.092402451973392294,"y":0.18895348867564266,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","w":0.81724848429361996},{"w":0.17324200948079432,"x":0.091980164569702816,"h":0.022538149673326902,"t":"Passage 1 below.","y":0.20524199682543942,"c":1},{"w":0.51129364013671874,"h":0.02193352465784304,"c":1,"x":0.25667350837148639,"t":"Archaeologists discover evidence of","y":0.24709302356537777},{"w":0.35783302307128906,"c":1,"t":"prehistoric island settlers","x":0.33235543875473561,"h":0.024636683281192395,"y":0.26912682528674714},{"c":1,"t":"In early April 2019, Dr Ceri Shipton and his colleagues from Australian National","x":0.09020396172697967,"w":0.74978988647460942,"y":0.30564665944276526,"h":0.025203307610345838},{"h":0.01902569120964126,"t":"University became the first archaeologists to explore Obi, one of many tropical islands","x":0.092402457956105855,"c":1,"y":0.32994186095989142,"w":0.81108830769856755},{"x":0.092319860858392347,"h":0.019621909262508064,"w":0.79073008219401042,"c":1,"t":"in Indonesia's Maluku Utara province. The research team's discoveries suggest that","y":0.34552504288012198},{"t":"the prehistoric people who lived on Obi were adept on both land and sea, hunting","x":0.090349087568048478,"h":0.017496741415828354,"w":0.7679671223958332,"c":1,"y":0.36627906979118197},{"h":0.01745901079656087,"y":0.38372093025613196,"t":"in the dense rainforest, foraging on the seashore, and possibly even voyaging","c":1,"w":0.73511291503906251,"x":0.09034908652564326},{"t":"between islands.","y":0.39964391712453307,"w":0.16283173878987628,"h":0.01763935145375306,"x":0.092125823087762349,"c":1},{"h":0.019050366336968771,"c":1,"w":0.80709238688151042,"t":"The excavations were part of a project to learn more about how people first dispersed","x":0.090305263936843974,"y":0.43576291945044421},{"w":0.75359344482421875,"x":0.090349068030163557,"c":1,"y":0.45486725680488926,"t":"from mainland Asia, through the Indonesian archipelago and into the prehistoric","h":0.016062975633109211},{"t":"continent that once connected Australia and New Guinea. The team's earlier research","x":0.090349063448898717,"y":0.47227138665098556,"h":0.016224188790560534,"c":1,"w":0.80903493245442715},{"y":0.48982558139915677,"w":0.8213552347819012,"c":1,"t":"suggested that the northernmost islands in the group, known as the Wallacean islands,","h":0.01754905003010343,"x":0.090349077328156585},{"c":1,"x":0.090349074559768122,"w":0.82135523478190098,"y":0.50726744182849481,"h":0.017511319410836168,"t":"including Obi, would have offered the easiest migration route. It also seemed likely that"},{"h":0.017473588228929082,"x":0.090349064207015883,"y":0.52470930234529067,"w":0.83367558797200525,"t":"these islands were crucial 'stepping stones' on humans' island-hopping voyages through","c":1},{"h":0.017457295870710654,"c":1,"x":0.090349063969721422,"w":0.82546203613281244,"y":0.54360465118643209,"t":"this region millennia ago. But to support this idea, they needed archaeological evidence"},{"y":0.56104651164894626,"w":0.83367558797200525,"t":"for humans living in this remote area in the ancient past. So, they travelled to Obi to look","h":0.017441860412777732,"x":0.090349064290359327,"c":1},{"h":0.015989229320424792,"w":0.52566736857096352,"x":0.090349067145045203,"c":1,"y":0.579941003116622,"t":"for sites that might reveal evidence of early occupation."},{"c":1,"t":"Just inland from the village of Kelo on Obi's northern coast, Shipton and his colleagues","y":0.61474926280944842,"w":0.81930185953776036,"h":0.016064690558959649,"x":0.09034907011883396},{"t":"found two caves containing prehistoric rock shelters that were suitable for excavation.","x":0.090349063445682234,"y":0.63215339209262067,"w":0.80903493245442704,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1},{"h":0.017547334541613391,"c":1,"w":0.73716634114583335,"t":"With the permission and help of the local people of Kelo, they dug a small test","y":0.64970930234932145,"x":0.090349067517432408},{"t":"excavation in each shelter. There they found numerous artefacts, including fragments","x":0.090263337058222634,"y":0.66586088321048953,"c":1,"h":0.02087325599692913,"w":0.80510375976562487},{"h":0.017493311564127589,"t":"of axes, some dating to about 14,000 years ago. The earliest axes at Kelo were made","w":0.80903493245442704,"c":1,"x":0.090349063424352116,"y":0.686046511651351},{"h":0.017526578199898668,"y":0.70342784437945283,"c":1,"x":0.090303765995283433,"t":"using clam shells. Axes made from clam shells from roughly the same time had also","w":0.79269851684570314},{"y":0.72093023258025246,"t":"previously been found elsewhere in this region, including on the nearby island of","c":1,"x":0.090349068374277794,"h":0.017441860412777732,"w":0.76180699666341145},{"c":1,"t":"Gebe to the northeast. As on Gebe, it is highly likely that Obi's axes were used in the","w":0.79683624267578124,"y":0.73776522802648381,"h":0.02037528158992441,"x":0.092342326563869315},{"w":0.77207392374674477,"c":1,"y":0.75722713887584903,"h":0.017482163420820651,"t":"construction of canoes, thus allowing these early peoples to maintain connections","x":0.090349074992692527},{"y":0.77463126850641706,"x":0.090349078516443818,"w":0.44763860066731775,"c":1,"h":0.017519894040088024,"t":"between communities on neighbouring islands."},{"c":1,"y":0.81091445401354878,"w":0.80698150634765631,"h":0.016224188790560423,"t":"The oldest cultural layers from the Kelo site provided the team with the earliest record","x":0.090349082452455223},{"t":"for human occupation on Obi, dating back around 18,000 years. At this time the climate","x":0.090349082941002246,"w":0.8234086100260416,"c":1,"h":0.017529327257544636,"y":0.82848837211630477},{"t":"was drier and colder than today, and the island's dense rainforests would likely have","x":0.090349069337377255,"y":0.84593023267327161,"w":0.79466120402018214,"h":0.016016669821950269,"c":1},{"w":0.78850102742513029,"h":0.015988371857499684,"x":0.090349075481013397,"y":0.86337209313375018,"c":1,"t":"been much less impenetrable than they are now. Sea levels were about 120 metres"},{"y":0.88081395329651824,"w":0.83162216186523441,"c":1,"h":0.017441860412777732,"x":0.088295694093050284,"t":"lower, meaning Obi was a much larger island, encompassing what is today the separate"},{"w":0.56900273640950527,"y":0.89805123572455792,"h":0.020609758315184856,"c":1,"t":"island of Bisa, as well as several other small islands nearby.","x":0.088179111859279777},{"h":0.013081394746943475,"w":0.026694043477376306,"x":0.090349076712714999,"c":1,"t":"62","y":0.92151162815341781},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.047780971470835598,"w":0.45180328369140621,"y":0.939023246385844,"c":1,"x":0.51825223579186064}],"w":2400}